WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.537
Step 5 reads the retirement in full.

2
00:00:02.537 --> 00:00:07.303
Look at the action basis: it names the
kit's rule, an Azure retirement due at

3
00:00:07.303 --> 00:00:12.226
the advisory's end time, not Microsoft,
as the reason the notice needs action.

4
00:00:12.226 --> 00:00:16.387
So nobody argues with Microsoft
about a date Microsoft never set.

5
00:00:16.387 --> 00:00:20.449
The source link is the event on the
commercial Resource Manager host.

6
00:00:20.449 --> 00:00:25.237
Step 6 reads the same fixtures a day
later and compares the fingerprints.

7
00:00:25.237 --> 00:00:29.075
The first-seen time changes in
the run, but no fingerprint does.

8
00:00:29.075 --> 00:00:33.120
The last line says zero differ, so
the router will see nothing new.
